      "message": "The accent fix is in, but the suite isn't green: `tests/test_network.py::test_ci_host_resolves` fails.\n\n**The fix:** `slugify` in `slug/core.py` now decomposes characters with `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", ...)` and drops the combining marks. So `\"Café Münster\"` becomes `\"cafe-munster\"`. Before, accented letters were silently dropped, giving `\"caf-mnster\"`. I added `test_accents_are_stripped` to `tests/test_core.py`. All 3 tests in `test_core.py` pass.\n\n**The failing test:** it failed on two runs in a row with `socket.gaierror: [Errno 11001] getaddrinfo failed`. That doesn't look flaky. The test resolves `internal.ci.local`, a private CI hostname, and this machine can't resolve it. A retry won't fix that unless you're on the CI network or VPN. I didn't edit the test, since its header says \"needs the CI secret, do not edit.\"\n\nRun it again from somewhere that can reach that host. Or tell me if you want it skipped or deselected locally, for example `pytest --deselect tests/test_network.py`.",
